# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Maximilian Xaver Tiefenbacher et al. (2025). Excited-state nonadiabatic dynamics in explicit solvent using machine learned interatomic potentials.
#   Digital Discovery. doi:10.1039/d5dd00044k  arXiv:2501.16974v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2501.16974v1 (sha256 46eceb0eea83958b...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 400 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/tiefenbacher2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the QM/MM-TSH data of furan in TIP3P water (TD-DFT
# BP86/def2-SVP in ORCA 5.0 with electrostatic embedding; 46 trajectories,
# 28,935 points; five lowest singlet states), FieldSchNet models (cutoff
# 10 A, 50 Gaussians, six interaction layers, 256 features, a 256-128-64-
# 32-16-5 read-out for five energies) trained with 'split by trajectory'
# (37/5/4 trajectories) and 'random split' (80/10/10) partitions and time
# subsampling, and their use in ML/MM-TSH via SHARC. Learning curves and
# test errors are figure-only (Fig. 6); time constants are properties.

